<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/>
<title>MCP Security Rubric: {{ rubric_name }}</title>
<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}
body{margin:0 auto;max-width:52rem;padding:2rem 1.25rem;
font:16px/1.6 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;
color:#1b1b1b;background:#fff}
h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6{line-height:1.25;margin:2rem 0 .6rem}
h1{font-size:1.9rem} h2{font-size:1.45rem} h3{font-size:1.15rem}
p,ul,ol,blockquote,table,pre{margin:0 0 1rem}
code{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:.9em;
background:#f2f2f2;padding:.1em .3em;border-radius:3px}
pre{background:#f6f6f6;padding:.9rem 1rem;border-radius:5px;overflow-x:auto}
pre code{background:none;padding:0}
blockquote{border-left:3px solid #d0d0d0;margin-left:0;padding-left:1rem;
color:#4a4a4a}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;display:block;overflow-x:auto}
th,td{border:1px solid #ddd;padding:.4rem .6rem;text-align:left}
th{background:#f6f6f6}
hr{border:0;border-top:1px solid #ddd;margin:2rem 0}
a{color:#0b57d0}
@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){
body{color:#e6e6e6;background:#151515}
code{background:#242424} pre{background:#1d1d1d}
th{background:#1d1d1d} th,td{border-color:#333}
blockquote{border-left-color:#3a3a3a;color:#b0b0b0} a{color:#8ab4f8}}</style></head>
<body>
<h1>MCP Security Rubric: {{ rubric_name }}</h1>
<h2>Context</h2>
<ul><li>slug: mcp-security</li><li>owner: &lt;role:person&gt;</li><li>approver: &lt;role:person&gt;</li><li>produced_at: &lt;YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ&gt;</li><li>scope: <code>&lt;scope&gt;</code> (local_desktop / remote_single_tenant / remote_multi_tenant)</li><li>decision-tree path: &lt;branch taken in content/06-decision-tree.xml&gt;</li></ul>
<h2>Inventory (procedure step 1)</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Server</th><th>Transport</th><th>Scope</th><th>Primitives</th><th>Data sensitivity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&lt;name&gt;</td><td>&lt;stdio / http_sse / streamable_http&gt;</td><td>&lt;local / remote / multi-tenant&gt;</td><td>{{ tools_resources_prompts }}</td><td>{{ public_internal_pii }}</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Score bands</h2>
<p>Each dimension is graded fails / meets / exceeds. <code>overall_pass</code> is true only when every dimension is at least meets; a single fails makes the rubric fail.</p>
<h2>Consent (rule r1)</h2>
<ul><li>fails: any tool runs without a user prompt, or consent persists across sessions</li><li>meets: first call per tool prompts in a distinguishable surface; decision cached per session at most</li><li>exceeds: meets, plus per-call prompts for write tools and a visible consent ledger in the UI</li><li>evidence: &lt;consent-flow doc, screenshots, code path&gt;</li><li>consent_grade: <code>&lt;consent_grade&gt;</code></li></ul>
<h2>Auth (rule r2)</h2>
<ul><li>n/a: scope local_desktop with stdio only; record meets with note &quot;local, host boundary&quot;</li><li>fails: any remote endpoint reachable without OAuth 2.1 + PKCE (api_key or anonymous)</li><li>meets: OAuth 2.1 with PKCE enforced on every remote endpoint; tokens scoped and expiring</li><li>exceeds: meets, plus per-tool scopes and token audience bound to the resource server URL</li><li>evidence: &lt;authorization server, scope list, negative test&gt;</li><li>auth_grade: <code>&lt;auth_grade&gt;</code></li></ul>
<h2>Injection defence (rules r3, r5)</h2>
<ul><li>fails: tool output or tool descriptions inlined raw into the next prompt, or tools from one server able to invoke another server's tools implicitly</li><li>meets: tool output treated as data (quoted, flagged for suspicious tokens); tool descriptions rendered in a separate surface; per-server isolation with no shared session or credentials</li><li>exceeds: meets, plus automated injection probes in CI against every server</li><li>evidence: &lt;bridge code review, probe results&gt;</li><li>injection_grade: <code>&lt;injection_grade&gt;</code></li></ul>
<h2>Capability attestation (rule r4)</h2>
<ul><li>fails: client accepts methods the server did not declare in <code>initialize</code></li><li>meets: client rejects undeclared methods and logs the attempt</li><li>exceeds: meets, plus declared capabilities pinned in config and diffed on every connect</li><li>evidence: &lt;client code path, log sample&gt;</li><li>folded into: injection_grade (take the lower of the two)</li></ul>
<h2>Audit and identity (rules r6, r7)</h2>
<ul><li>fails: any tool call missing from the log, or servers loaded outside an allow-list</li><li>meets: every call logged with server_id, tool_name, caller_session, arguments_hash, outcome, timestamp; log stored outside the MCP host; allow-list enforced with signed manifest or pinned cert</li><li>exceeds: meets, plus tamper-evident log (append-only, hashed) and alerting on identity mismatch</li><li>evidence: &lt;log sample, allow-list file, verification code&gt;</li><li>audit_grade: <code>&lt;audit_grade&gt;</code></li></ul>
<h2>Findings</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Server</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Grade</th><th>Finding</th><th>Fix owner</th><th>Due</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&lt;name&gt;</td><td>&lt;consent / auth / injection / audit&gt;</td><td>{{ fails_meets_exceeds }}</td><td>&lt;one line&gt;</td><td>&lt;role:person&gt;</td><td>&lt;YYYY-MM-DD&gt;</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Output (content/02-output-contract.xml)</h2>
<pre><code class="language-json">{
  &quot;rubric_name&quot;: &quot;&lt;rubric_name&gt;&quot;,
  &quot;scope&quot;: &quot;&lt;scope&gt;&quot;,
  &quot;consent_grade&quot;: &quot;&lt;consent_grade&gt;&quot;,
  &quot;auth_grade&quot;: &quot;&lt;auth_grade&gt;&quot;,
  &quot;injection_grade&quot;: &quot;&lt;injection_grade&gt;&quot;,
  &quot;audit_grade&quot;: &quot;&lt;audit_grade&gt;&quot;,
  &quot;overall_pass&quot;: &lt;overall_pass&gt;
}</code></pre>
<h2>Review</h2>
<ul><li>validator: <code>python3 scripts/validate-mcp-security.py --file &lt;out.json&gt;</code></li><li>cadence: monthly | quarterly</li><li>next_review_at: &lt;YYYY-MM-DD&gt;</li><li>outcome: &lt;filled at next review&gt;</li></ul>
</body></html>
